1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
miss = real − guess.

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:03,200
But what if the dots DON'T line up?

3
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:05,600
Four days of sales: 30, 45, 50, 65.

4
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:08,000
Last time the dots sat perfectly on a line.

5
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,400
These don't. So which line is right?

6
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:12,800
Try one — the line from last time.

7
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:15,200
Day 2. The line says 40. The shop sold 45.

8
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:17,600
Real goes up into the equation. So does guess.

9
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:20,000
That gap is the miss. 5.

10
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,400
Now every day. The misses are 0, 5, 0, 5.

11
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:24,800
A dot below counts the same as above — so square them.

12
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:27,200
Total miss = 50. One number for how wrong the WHOLE line is.

13
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:29,600
Tilt it, and watch that number.

14
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:31,200
50 down to 20. A better line.

15
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:32,800
It misses all four a little, instead of two badly. That IS training.

16
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:34,000
We learned this at school.

17
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:35,200
Nobody ever said what for.

18
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:36,800
Send this to your school friend — and tell them THIS is how it's solved.

19
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:40,000
Follow for the math behind AI. @observer.collapse
